## §3 T1 — the source test (decisive, and not what A8 predicted)

SAEOS-1 §6.1b specifies the emission bundle by naming, for each node type, the PAEOS
artifact it is extracted *from*. Every one of those artifacts was searched for, for all
three goals:

| §6.1b emission | Named source | Present for B0.0 / B0.1 / B0.2? |
|---|---|---|
| `Decision` | the decision-graph (ADR records + `constitutional_basis`) | **absent** — `ledger/` contains only `debt/`; no `ledger/decisions/` exists |
| `TradeOff` | the L06 trade-off matrix | **absent** — no trade-off matrix exists anywhere outside `backlog/research/` |
| `Option` | L04 candidates, including rejected | **absent** — no candidate architecture set for any B0.x goal |
| `Constraint` | the L11 implementation contract | **absent** — no implementation contract artifact |
| `Component` | the L08 architecture artifact set | **absent** — `architecture/` contains only `invariants.json` |
| `Scar` | the scar-graph (root-cause bundle, A-10) | **absent** — no scar-graph on disk |
| `EvidenceRef` | hashes from PAEOS's CAS | **absent** — no `artifact_hash`/`env_hash` recorded in any sealed review |

**7 of 7 named sources do not exist.** An extractor implemented literally against §6.1b
returns an empty bundle for every one of these goals: `loss_ratio_as_written: 1.000`.

This is not sloppiness on the goals' part. `operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md` (FROZEN
v1.0) defines **ceremony depth**: Trace-A "auto-discharges L03–L11 … each records a machine
'auto-pass, Trace-A' evidence stub". L04, L06, L07, L08 and L11 — five of the six sources
above — sit inside the auto-discharged band. For any goal not routed Trace-B, those
artifacts are **stubs by constitutional design**. §6.1b sources the emission bundle from
the exact lifecycle range the lifecycle is entitled to skip.

Worse for reproducibility: **no L02 ceremony-depth record exists for any B0.x goal**, so an
extractor cannot even determine which artifacts it is entitled to expect, or distinguish
"legitimately auto-discharged" from "missing".

What *does* exist per sealed goal is five artifacts — the PAEOS-8 §11 task row, the
`reviews/tasks/` L17 review, the off-contract `docs/` review, the CER-3 debt entry, and the
module docstring. **None of the five is named in §6.1b.** §6.1b's producer map is wrong in
both directions: it names sources that do not exist and omits every source that does.

## §4 T2 — the content test: scoring method

Because T1 alone forces the verdict, T2 was run anyway to answer the *next* question the
founder gate needs: if §6.1b's source map were corrected to point at the artifacts that do
exist, how much survives?

**Unit.** One *slot* = (node type × content-bearing field). Scope is the seven node types
§6.1b puts in the S1 bundle.

**Fields scored (content-bearing only).** Nine shared envelope fields from SAEOS-1 §4.2 —
`label`, `summary`, `provenance.origin`, `provenance.source_hash`, `evidence[]`,
`valid_from`, `valid_until`, `falsifier`, `coordinates` — plus type payload:
Decision 5 (`problem_context`, `chosen`, `alternatives_considered`, `rationale`,
`constitutional_basis`) · TradeOff 4 (`axis`, `side_a`, `side_b`, `resolution`) ·
Option 3 · Constraint 3 · Component 3 (`element_kind`, `interface`, `dependency_edges`) ·
Scar 3 (`root_cause`, `detection_signature`, `guard_action`) · EvidenceRef 4
(`hash`, `uri`, `kind`, `reverification_instructions`).

**Deliberately excluded from the denominator** — the seven envelope fields the extractor
*mints* rather than extracts (`id`, `type`, `namespace`, `provenance.author_kind`,
`provenance.ingested_at`, `status`, `confidence`), and `facets` (no facet is registered at
v1). Counting minted fields as "extractable" is the specific way this probe could have
flattered itself into a GO; they are excluded on purpose. `confidence` is excluded under
§4.2's own invariant that it is derived, never authored.

**Scale.** extractable = 1.0 · partial = 0.5 · absent = 0.0.
**Totals.** 88 slots per goal (14+13+12+12+12+12+13), 264 across the corpus.
`loss_ratio = 1 − (Σ score ÷ 264)`.

**On "structurally absent".** No node type was scored `n/a`. Each of the seven was checked
for whether the goal genuinely had nothing to say (which would be an unfair loss) versus
had something to say that the artifact failed to capture (a real loss). In all 21 cases the
material existed in some form — including B0.2's `Scar`, which is the sharpest cell in the
probe (§5.3). The denominator is therefore never shrunk in SAKG's favour.

